# A holding that answers back (owner 2026-09-17, docs/VISION.md §9.5), on the
# real keys: an armed turret in the yard, a body coming for the place, the gun
# coming round onto it, the bolts, and the switch that stands it down again —
# because a turret armed is stolen technology humming in the walls, and running
# dark is an answer too.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/turret.tour --seed=1 --hour=10 --weather=clear:0 \
#     --holding=hut,wind_spinner,battery_stack,battery_stack,turret --fail-downed
#
# (--holding stands the yard already built, its cells full: putting a turret up
# is the holding app's proof and settlements.tour's. This one starts at the
# moment it matters.)
coast calm
wait 0.8
shot 01-an-armed-turret-in-the-yard with holding, piece:turret, turret_armed
# Something comes for the place. It is pressing a fight, so the gun takes it.
spawn runner
wait 0.2
shot 02-something-comes-for-the-yard with mob:runner
await turret_target 8
wait 0.35
shot 03-the-gun-comes-round with mob:runner, turret_target
await turret_hit 10
shot 04-the-yard-answers-back with turret_hit
until turret_kill 20
wait 0.6
shot 05-after with turret_fired
# The switch: a live gun is stood down before anything else is done to it, and
# the page says what the key will do before it is pressed.
coast calm
tap holding
await app:holding 4
choose piece_5
wait 0.4
shot 06-armed-on-the-page with app:holding, turret_armed
tap use
wait 0.5
shot 07-stood-down with app:holding
tap pause
